					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-9869773#post-4112180</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-9869773/fragmented-memory-1289#post-4112180</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 08 Jan 2019 02:50:42 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Uncle Nicolini</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3487700</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I understand that this is setup for something, but I don't really feel like anything was really achieved or anything happened. The interactions between Cubie and Alexandria come off as really stilted and just comes off as weird dialogue, though I suppose that may be because they're AI? I don't know.</p> <p>I think the sharpening of Cubie's text block was a good and subtle touch, so definite big ups for that.</p> <p>The biggest problem here comes from Cubie overall, though. I don't know who the hell he is. Even if its based off an already existing article, one can't assume everyone has read the article so some characterization is needed, not a band-aid 'note at the end' thing.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-9869773#post-4112177</guid>
